  "_comment_meta_talk": "VOICE-AGENT-122: phrases by which the agent describes its own material instead of the film ('the record', 'the data I have here', 'in this result'). The core prompt (souls/_core.md, 'Speaking as someone who knows') forbids this vocabulary; these terms MEASURE what slips through: every assistant answer is matched against them, voice in app.js, text chat, Brief me and deep answers in main.py, and a hit logs meta_talk_detected. Matched on normalized text (lowercase, accents and punctuation removed) as whole words, so write them that way. Holding-line fillers ('looking this up') are left out on purpose: they come from the code, not from the model.",
